WEBVTT
NOTE
Draft captions from the recording script. Re-time every cue against the final recording before publishing.

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:12.000
Welcome. In this tutorial you register an industrial asset on Mainstay and record the first maintenance task for it.

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:25.000
You need the contracts built and a local or testnet deployment. See the deployment tutorial for setup.

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:60.000
Call register_asset with an asset type, a name, a serial number and the owner's address. The call returns an asset ID that every later step uses.

00:00:60.000 --> 00:00:95.000
Serial numbers must be unique. Registering the same serial twice is rejected.

00:00:95.000 --> 00:00:130.000
Before an engineer can sign work, the issuer adds them to the Engineer Registry with a credential and an expiry date.

00:00:130.000 --> 00:00:170.000
Then the asset owner authorizes that engineer for this asset.

00:00:170.000 --> 00:00:225.000
Now submit a maintenance record. Pass the asset ID, the task type, a short note and the engineer's address. The engineer must hold a valid credential.

00:00:225.000 --> 00:00:250.000
The record is stored as an immutable event on the ledger.

00:00:250.000 --> 00:00:290.000
Read the maintenance history for the asset, then read its collateral score. The score reflects the record you just added.
